    "q-79745": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79745",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Given a rectangular pyramid, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ of the rectangular pyramid if the base is a square with the side of $a=6$ and the height is $h=5.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume of the rectangular pyramid is $V=\\frac{1}{3}{a}^{2}h.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(a,h) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{2ah}{3}\\,\\text{d}a+\\frac{{a}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=6$ and $h=5,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(6,5) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 6\\cdot 5}{3}\\,\\text{d}a+\\frac{{6}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =20\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
