    "q-37306": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37306",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+y,$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y)$ from $(4\\pi ,8)$ to $(13,8.5).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(4\\pi ,8),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(4\\pi ,8) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\pi \\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(4\\pi +Δx,8+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+1\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(4\\pi ,8)$ to $(13,8.5),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =13-4\\pi , \\\\ Δy & =8.5-8=0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\,Δx+1\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈0\\cdot (13-4\\pi )+1\\cdot (0.5) \\\\  & ≈0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $0.5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
